WEBVTT

NOTE How to download and save your goodies on a computer. Captions follow the narration.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.448
Hi there!

2
00:00:01.548 --> 00:00:05.793
In this video, I'll show you how to download your goodies on a computer,

3
00:00:05.793 --> 00:00:09.331
save them somewhere easy to find, and find them again later.

4
00:00:10.881 --> 00:00:12.387
First, let's sign in.

5
00:00:12.487 --> 00:00:15.788
Click the person icon at the top right of any page.

6
00:00:17.138 --> 00:00:20.000
Enter the email and password for your account.

7
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.536
Then click Sign in.

8
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.572
Your account opens.

9
00:00:24.672 --> 00:00:26.504
Click the My downloads tab.

10
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.562
Each purchase has its own card, with the order number and the version.

11
00:00:32.662 --> 00:00:35.652
When it's ready, it says one download available.

12
00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:39.863
Before you download, here's the important part.

13
00:00:39.963 --> 00:00:44.398
Each digital purchase includes one download of the latest version.

14
00:00:44.498 --> 00:00:48.426
Starting the download uses it. Just looking at this page doesn't.

15
00:00:48.526 --> 00:00:52.157
And when a new version comes out, you'll get one new download of it.

16
00:00:53.507 --> 00:00:56.540
When you're ready to save it, click Download on the card.

17
00:00:59.007 --> 00:01:00.561
A reminder pops up.

18
00:01:00.661 --> 00:01:02.780
Read it, then click Download now.

19
00:01:04.507 --> 00:01:07.611
A message lets you know your download has started.

20
00:01:07.711 --> 00:01:11.064
From here, your browser saves the file to your computer.

21
00:01:12.414 --> 00:01:15.478
Most browsers save files to your Downloads folder.

22
00:01:15.578 --> 00:01:19.488
If your browser asks where to save it, pick a folder you'll remember.

23
00:01:19.588 --> 00:01:24.453
Tip: keep all your inserts together in one folder, like one named Nurse Love.

24
00:01:25.803 --> 00:01:29.060
To find it again on Windows, open File Explorer,

25
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.181
then click Downloads, or the folder you chose.

26
00:01:32.281 --> 00:01:36.230
On a Mac, open Finder, then click Downloads in the sidebar.

27
00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:42.061
Back on the website, My downloads now says Download used, with the date.

28
00:01:42.161 --> 00:01:46.399
The website can't see your computer, so it can't tell whether the file saved.

29
00:01:46.499 --> 00:01:49.594
So open the file once, just to make sure it's there.

30
00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:55.771
If the file didn't save, or it won't open, click Report a download problem.

31
00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:59.092
A real person at the store reads every report.

32
00:02:00.442 --> 00:02:04.210
For anything else, click Support in your account and send a message.

33
00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.000
You'll hear back by email.

34
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.378
And that's it!

35
00:02:08.478 --> 00:02:12.732
Download once, save it somewhere easy to find, and open it to check.

36
00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.247
Thanks for watching.
